{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1647"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1647: acquireLock / acquireLockLease follow a symlinked locks directory and create the lock outside the tracker"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1647 (found by pm-rl's state-confinement guarantee, unbraind/pm-rl#107): when the tracker's locks directory (or a lock entry's parent) is a symlink, acquireLock and acquireLockLease follow it and create the lock outside the tracker, so two writers resolving the path differently share no exclusion point and an extension cannot close the check/use window with its own pathname check. The SDK must refuse a symlinked or swapped lock directory with a typed lock_path_unsafe error and never create a lock outside the tracker."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["bug","concurrency","gh:1647","locks","sdk","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"acquireLock and acquireLockLease refuse with code lock_path_unsafe when the tracker's locks directory, or any component between the tracker root and the lock entry, is a symlink or not a directory, and no file is created outside the tracker; a swap of the locks directory between the confinement check and lock creation is detected by comparing the created lock's identity with the confined directory entry, the stray lock is removed, and the acquisition refuses with lock_path_unsafe; regression tests cover a pre-existing symlinked locks directory and a swap during acquisition for both acquireLock and acquireLockLease; the refusal is documented in docs/SDK.md"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-dj98"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Locks are created only inside the tracker; a symlinked or swapped locks directory refuses with a typed lock_path_unsafe error and leaves nothing outside the tracker."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"acquireLock(\".agents/pm\", \"probe\", ...) with .agents/pm/locks symlinked to ./outside creates outside/probe.lock and returns a working release function."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1576","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-zwib","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"text=Intake for GH-1647. Duplicate check: pm search 'symlink lock confinement' (pm-d70h, pm-nkx, pm-zwib, pm-fsyv, pm-lxa0, pm-gh1609 are all closed and cover TTL, stale takeover, extension-entry symlinks and include-linked containment, not the locks directory itself); pm list --status open/in_progress shows no lock-confinement item. Related: pm-gh1576 closes a different check/use window (expected item revisions)."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6cba5dcb65b5e6af1f1299ea86add89ea4a8a07c034cbc1b5bd1c07ba0975863","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6f2e4d26c0433a50bff6716bbf29e885e18fa759895c124ca55493ff6041c7f4"}
